---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const exampleResource = `---
title: Intro to SQL — Querying and managing data
provider: Khan Academy
url: https://www.khanacademy.org/computing/computer-programming/sql
description: Interactive SQL taught in the browser — queries, aggregation,
  joins and modifying databases — with talk-throughs and challenges.
subjects: [data, programming]
level: beginner
format: interactive
language: en
---`;
---

<Layout
  title="Contribute — Cassandra Open Education"
  description="Cassandra is built by people passing on the route they took. Add a resource, improve a path, or vet links — no coding required for most of it."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h1>Contribute</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Every path on Cassandra exists because someone who found the way passed the route on. All
        the content is plain text files in a
        <a href="https://github.com/the-muses-ltd/Cassandra">public GitHub repository</a> — if you
        can edit a text file, you can contribute.
      </p>

      <h2>The quality bar</h2>
      <p>Before proposing a resource, check it against the bar every reviewer will use:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Genuinely free to learn from.</strong> Free trials, "first module free" and
          audit-only-with-nagging don't qualify. A free account requirement or an optional paid
          certificate is acceptable if we say so in the resource's notes.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Excellent, not merely acceptable.</strong> The library is a shortlist, not a
          search engine. Would you recommend it to a friend over every alternative?
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Likely to last.</strong> Established institutions, foundations and long-running
          community projects — not a personal blog that may vanish next year.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Add a resource</h2>
      <p>
        A resource is one markdown file in <code>src/content/resources/</code>. Copy an existing one
        or start from this template, then open a pull request:
      </p>
      <pre><code>{exampleResource}</code></pre>
      <p>
        The build validates every field, and a maintainer reviews every submission before it goes
        live — that review, in the open, is our whole editorial process.
      </p>

      <h2>Improve or propose a path</h2>
      <p>
        Paths live in <code>src/content/paths/</code> — ordered stages, each with resources, a
        rationale and a checkpoint. The most valuable contributions come from people who recently
        walked the route themselves: you still remember where you got lost.
      </p>
      <p>Paths we want next: mathematics from arithmetic to calculus, basic digital literacy, and
        paths in languages other than English.</p>

      <h2>No pull request required</h2>
      <p>
        Not comfortable with GitHub?
        <a href="https://github.com/the-muses-ltd/Cassandra/issues">Open an issue</a> describing the
        resource or the problem, and someone will turn it into a change. Link-checking, testing
        paths as a real learner, and translating are all contributions we need just as much as code.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
